{"at":"2026-11-23T17:12:14.633Z","round":1,"event":"write","id":"options_chat_pace_preview","ok":true,"cost_usd":0.7432677,"turns":16,"summary":"I added `previewChatPace()` to `src/scenes/OptionsScene.js`, but it is untested: I wasn't allowed to run `npm run boot-test` or even a syntax check, so neither has run. The harness's boot test will be the first check.\n\nThe PREVIEW panel's single still message is now a chat area that plays Liam, Mina and Cyrus. Each speaker's \"is typing\" row lasts `chatPaceMs()`, then their message appears. After the last line it waits 2 s, clears and starts again. Rows are smaller than in the real chat so the review and stars still fit, and the area scrolls to the newest line if Large text makes it overflow. Changing Chat pace redraws the screen, so the new pace starts straight away. With Animations off the timing is the same but lines just appear. The timer stops when you leave Options. `previewMotion()` now only animates the stars, because the old sliding bubble is gone.\n\nFiles changed: `src/scenes/OptionsScene.js` and `CLAUDE.md` (one new bullet in \"Decisions taken in the prototype\", ending \"(feature agent, 2026-11-23)\")."}
