{"at":"2026-11-23T17:27:55.703Z","round":1,"event":"write","id":"font_sets","ok":true,"cost_usd":1.6829898,"turns":54,"summary":"I've built the font sets, but I couldn't check them: this session wasn't allowed to run any commands, so `npm run boot-test` and my both-font-set screenshot check of every screen never ran. All six done-conditions are met, since the four `@fontsource` packages were already in `package.json`. The default set is Silkscreen + Nunito, and \"Easier reading\" (a new Font row in Options) switches to Jersey 10 + Lexend.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **Fonts:** `src/main.js` now loads all four fonts and waits for them before the game starts. Jersey 10 only comes in one weight, so it has no bold. Pixelify Sans is no longer imported.\n- **Font choice:** the text-style helpers in `src/ui/theme.js` look up the chosen set each time they're called, so a change shows as each screen redraws. Headings use the 0.82 (Silkscreen) and 1.3 (Jersey 10) size factors. The setting itself is in `src/ui/settings.js`.\n- **Two direct font uses:** `src/ui/badge.js` and `src/ui/widgets.js` named Pixelify Sans themselves, so I switched them to the new helpers.\n- **Spilling text:** since I couldn't look at the screens, I added a `fitWidth()` helper that shrinks a one-line label until it fits its box. It's used on every button label, the venue card names (`ResultsListScene.js`), the map's district labels (`cityMap.js`), the Chat header (`ChatScene.js`), and the Outcome title and \"You sent everyone to…\" line (`OutcomeScene.js`). Other fixed text, like the menu district card and the Friends page names, should fit by my estimate but isn't protected.\n- **Options:** `OptionsScene.js` has six rows again (each row 84 px tall). The description text moved up slightly, because in Lexend some descriptions could wrap to two lines and nearly touch the bottom of their row.\n- **Notes:** `game/CLAUDE.md` has the updated \"Palette and fonts\" line and a new \"Font sets\" bullet.\n\nBefore relying on it, please look at Options, the restaurant list and the Outcome screen in both font sets, ideally with Large text on too."}
