{"at":"2026-11-23T17:41:17.032Z","round":1,"event":"write","id":"one_font_set","ok":true,"cost_usd":0.7951638000000001,"turns":24,"summary":"I've switched the game to one font set, but I couldn't run `npm run boot-test` because the permission prompt for it wasn't approved. The harness's run will be the first test.\n\nAll five done-checks should now hold. Jersey 10 is used for headings and buttons and Lexend for chat and reviews, and nothing in `src/` names Silkscreen, Nunito, `fontChoice` or the Font row any more.\n\nFiles changed:\n- **`src/ui/theme.js`**: `FONT_SETS` and the per-set lookup are gone. The fonts are now fixed, with the old fallbacks after each one. Jersey 10's ×1.3 size factor stays inside `pixel()`, and `fitWidth()` is kept.\n- **`src/ui/settings.js`**: the font setting, its options, its default and `fontChoice()` are removed. A font value from an older save is simply ignored.\n- **`src/scenes/OptionsScene.js`**: the Font row is removed. I restored the five-row spacing from before font_sets (rows 100 px tall, description at +38 with normal line spacing), so keyboard focus covers the five rows that are left. The Preview now shows Jersey 10 + Lexend.\n- **`src/main.js`**: imports only the Jersey 10 400 and Lexend 400/700 CSS, and waits only for those two families.\n- **`game/CLAUDE.md`**: I updated the Palette and fonts line, rewrote the Font sets bullet as a \"Fonts\" bullet, and added a \"One font set\" bullet ending \"(feature agent, 2026-11-23)\".\n\n`package.json` is unchanged, so it still lists `@fontsource/silkscreen` and `@fontsource/nunito` for you to uninstall."}
