{"at":"2026-11-24T15:39:32.182Z","round":2,"event":"write","id":"ending_seen_on_leave","ok":true,"cost_usd":0.5251212999999999,"turns":13,"summary":"The ending now counts as seen only when the player leaves it, but I couldn't run `npm run boot-test`: this session wasn't allowed to run it. It still needs to run before this is committed.\n\n**What changed in `src/scenes/EndingScene.js`:**\n- `create()` no longer calls `markEndingSeen()`.\n- `leave()` now calls it just before going back to the map. That covers Continue, Enter or → on part 2, and Esc or Backspace on part 2.\n- Skipping part 1 with Esc still goes to part 2 without marking the ending as seen.\n- If the player reloads or closes the tab partway through the ending, `lets-eat-ending-seen-v1` stays unset. The next perfect level_20 pick offers \"Continue →\" to the ending again.\n\nI also added one bullet to the \"Decisions taken in the prototype\" list in `game/CLAUDE.md`, ending with \"(feature agent, 2026-11-24)\". `src/scenes/EndingScene.js` and `CLAUDE.md` are the only files I changed."}
