{"at":"2026-11-24T15:42:51.117Z","round":3,"event":"write","id":"reset_clears_seen_memory","ok":true,"cost_usd":0.5726117000000002,"turns":17,"summary":"I added an exported `clearSeen()` to `src/ui/chapterIntro.js`, `src/ui/howToPlay.js` and `src/ui/friendsAnnounced.js`, and `resetProgress()` in `src/ui/widgets.js` now calls all three. Each one empties its module's in-memory \"seen\" list and removes its saved key. That memory copy is what kept How to play, the chapter cards and the new-friend cards hidden after a reset until the page was reloaded. `resetProgress()` no longer removes those three keys itself. I also added the decision bullet to `game/CLAUDE.md`. I couldn't run `npm run boot-test` because permission was refused, so the change is untested. I also didn't re-run the bug hunter's SF-01 script. All four \"done\" checks now match. `howToPlay.js` already imported `widgets.js`, so the two files now import each other. That should be harmless because the imports are only used inside functions, but the harness's boot test will confirm it."}
