{"at":"2026-11-24T15:50:09.950Z","round":5,"event":"write","id":"kb_chat_star","ok":true,"cost_usd":0.7997332,"turns":17,"summary":"Chat lines can now be starred by keyboard in levels from chapter 2 on. **I couldn't run `npm run boot-test`** because the command wasn't approved here, so the change is untested. I also couldn't open the KB-03 bug report on `master`, so I haven't checked the bug hunter's script against it. Both files I changed are in the `game` folder:\n\n- **`src/scenes/ChatScene.js`**:\n  - In star levels, ↑/↓ move a focus ring through the lines shown so far. The ring starts on the newest line, and the chat scrolls to keep it in view.\n  - S (`keydown-S`) stars or unstars the focused line. Clicking a star and pressing S use the same code. If no line is focused, S first focuses the newest line and stars it.\n  - Both keys do nothing while the volume panel or an intro card is open.\n  - The key hint now says \"↑ ↓: pick a line · s: star a line\".\n  - In star levels ↑/↓ no longer scroll by a step. Page Up/Down and Home/End still scroll. Chapter 1 keeps its old arrow scrolling and hint.\n- **`CLAUDE.md`**: added one bullet for this feature, ending \"(feature agent, 2026-11-24)\"."}
