{"at":"2026-11-24T15:53:55.527Z","round":6,"event":"write","id":"kb_options_reset","ok":true,"cost_usd":0.7474813,"turns":13,"summary":"I added keyboard access to Reset progress on the Options screen, but I couldn't run any checks. `npm run boot-test` and a plain `node --check` syntax check both needed permissions this session doesn't have, so the change is untested. I also couldn't rerun the bug hunter's script for KB-02: its report is on `master` (`logs/bughunt/`) and isn't in this worktree.\n\n**What now works in `src/scenes/OptionsScene.js`:**\n- **Reaching the button:** ↑ ↓ now go through the setting rows and then the Reset progress button, wrapping round. R jumps straight to it, and a highlight ring shows when it has focus.\n- **Opening the check:** Enter on the button opens the \"Reset progress?\" check.\n- **Inside the check:** focus starts on Cancel and a ring marks the focused button. ← picks Cancel, → picks Reset, Enter presses the focused one and Esc cancels.\n- **Safety:** the check's keys wait one tick after it opens, so the Enter that opened it can't press anything. They also do nothing while the volume panel is open.\n- **Key hint:** it now names R.\n\nThe `resetFocus` match is in place. One older rule has changed: Enter used to never reset. Now it resets only when Reset has focus.\n\nI added one bullet to `game/CLAUDE.md` describing this. Those two files are the only ones I changed."}
