{"at":"2026-11-24T15:57:30.245Z","round":7,"event":"write","id":"kb_results_sort_filter","ok":true,"cost_usd":0.7115774,"turns":18,"summary":"On the restaurant list, S now cycles the sort (Mixed → Cheapest → A–Z) and F cycles the filters (all → each SHOW chip on its own, in order → all). Both work exactly like clicking the buttons, but I couldn't run any checks: `npm run boot-test` and even a plain `node --check` were refused for permission in this session. The harness's boot-test run will be the first test of this code. I also couldn't read the bug hunter's KB-04 report on `master`, so I haven't confirmed that its script no longer reproduces the bug.\n\n- **Keys:** both keys do nothing while the volume panel is open, and F does nothing when a level has no filter row.\n- **Open place:** it stays open unless a filter hides it. Then it closes, the same as with a click.\n- **Focus ring:** it stays on the open place, otherwise on the card that had focus before, otherwise the first card. Before, it went back to the first card whenever nothing was open.\n- **Key hint:** the bottom text now includes \"s: sort\", plus \"f: filter\" when the level has filter buttons.\n\nI changed two files: `src/scenes/ResultsListScene.js` (the S and F keys, a small helper listing the filter buttons in on-screen order, the focus behaviour and the key hint) and `CLAUDE.md` (one new bullet under \"Decisions taken in the prototype\")."}
