{"at":"2026-11-24T16:02:04.172Z","round":8,"event":"write","id":"kb_volume_panel","ok":true,"cost_usd":1.0656211,"turns":28,"summary":"I've made the volume panel work from the keyboard, but I couldn't run `npm run boot-test` or a plain syntax check: this session wasn't allowed to approve any commands. I also didn't run the bug hunter's script for KB-05/KB-06, because its report and script aren't in this worktree. The harness's boot test will be the first real run.\n\n**What the panel does now:** M opens or closes it. While it's open, ← → change the volume in 10% steps, Enter or Space turns Music on or off (the Options \"Music\" row follows), and Esc or M closes it. Every other key is held back too, so nothing reaches the chat, Options or the restaurant list underneath.\n\n**Why keys leaked before:** the music panel's top layer (`HudScene`) used Phaser's `stopImmediatePropagation()`, which only stops its own handlers and still lets the screens underneath see the key. It now uses `stopPropagation()`, which stops the key there. The `hudPanelOpen` flag the screens already check stays as a backup.\n\n**Files changed:**\n- `src/scenes/HudScene.js`: the keys above, including `keydown-LEFT` and `keydown-RIGHT`.\n- `src/scenes/ChatScene.js`, `src/scenes/ResultsListScene.js`, `src/scenes/OptionsScene.js`: \"m: music\" added to the key hints. I tightened the separators on Chat and Options so the longer hints still fit.\n- `CLAUDE.md` in the game folder: one new bullet ending \"(feature agent, 2026-11-24)\"."}
