{"at":"2026-11-24T16:09:30.757Z","round":10,"event":"write","id":"map_opens_on_played_level","ok":true,"cost_usd":0.7451546,"turns":16,"summary":"The map now opens on the district and level card you just played. I haven't run `npm run boot-test`, because this session wasn't allowed to run npm commands, so the change is untested until the harness runs it. I also couldn't read the bug hunter's NP-01 and KB-10 reports (access to the `logs/bughunt` files on master was blocked), so I haven't checked the change against their script. When a level's chat opens, `src/scenes/ChatScene.js` saves it in the registry as `lastLevel`. It skips this for the How to play demo opened from Options, since that isn't a real play. The next time the map opens, `src/scenes/MenuScene.js` selects that level's district and puts the focus ring on its card. It does this once per level visit, so a district you pick afterwards still sticks when you come back from Options or another screen. I added a bullet for this to the \"Decisions taken in the prototype\" list in `game/CLAUDE.md`."}
