{"at":"2026-11-24T16:13:11.226Z","round":11,"event":"write","id":"options_music_row_sync","ok":true,"cost_usd":0.7528120999999999,"turns":17,"summary":"The Options screen's Music row now follows the bottom-left music button, but I couldn't run `npm run boot-test`: the permission check blocked the command. I also couldn't read the bug hunter's SF-02 report (that command was blocked too), so I haven't checked that its script no longer reproduces the bug. The harness's own boot-test run will be the first test of this change.\n\nI changed three files:\n- **`src/scenes/OptionsScene.js`**: a new `syncMusicRow` handler listens for music changes while Options is open. When the music button switches music on or off, it saves the new setting and redraws the screen straight away, keeping the keyboard focus. Choosing \"On\" on the row afterwards works again (before, the row still thought \"On\" was selected and did nothing). Volume changes and the row's own choice don't cause a redraw.\n- **`src/ui/music.js`**: `onVolume()` now returns a function that stops listening, so Options removes its listener when you leave the screen.\n- **`CLAUDE.md`**: one new bullet in \"Decisions taken in the prototype\", ending \"(feature agent, 2026-11-24)\".\n\nIf the music button is used while the \"Reset progress?\" check is open, the redraw closes that check. Nothing is reset when this happens."}
