{"at":"2026-11-24T16:16:14.602Z","round":12,"event":"write","id":"outcome_focus_try_again","ok":true,"cost_usd":0.5084188000000001,"turns":8,"summary":"After a fail, the Outcome screen's focus ring now starts on \"Try again\", so Enter retries instead of going back to the map. I couldn't run `npm run boot-test`, because the command needed an approval this session can't give, and I didn't rerun the bug hunter's script for this bug, so nothing here is tested yet. The change is in `src/scenes/OutcomeScene.js`: a new `const defaultFocus` picks \"Try again\" after a fail (before, focus started on the last button, \"Levels\"). After a partial or perfect pick it picks the green continue button (Next level →, Continue → or Back to levels), which is the same button that was focused before. I also added one bullet for this fix to the \"Decisions taken in the prototype\" list in `game/CLAUDE.md`, ending with \"(feature agent, 2026-11-24)\"."}
