{"at":"2026-11-24T16:19:23.623Z","round":13,"event":"write","id":"page_centred_brown_bars","ok":true,"cost_usd":0.547369,"turns":10,"summary":"I changed two files. In `game/index.html`, the page background is now the game's dark brown `#2e2624` (C.bg, was `#2b2233`), so the done check passes. The flex centring on `#game` is gone, so only Phaser's `CENTER_BOTH` in `src/main.js` centres the canvas. Centring it in both places applied the offset twice, which made the side bars uneven. I also added `overflow: hidden` and `canvas { display: block }` so no scrollbar or stray gap appears. `src/main.js` didn't need changing. In `game/CLAUDE.md` I added an AX-01 bullet to the \"Decisions taken in the prototype\" list. I couldn't run `npm run boot-test` because the command needed approval that wasn't given, so the harness's run will be the first check. I also didn't re-run the bug hunter's AX-01 script, so nothing has confirmed yet that a 1280x720 or 800x1000 window now shows equal bars."}
