{"at":"2026-11-24T16:23:08.134Z","round":14,"event":"write","id":"speaker_names_readable","ok":true,"cost_usd":0.8541346,"turns":29,"summary":"Speaker names on the Outcome screen and the Ending now get their colour from a new `nameColor()`, but I couldn't run `npm run boot-test`: it needs approval that this session can't grant, so the harness's run will be the first check. I also didn't run the bug hunter's AX-04 script, because the report on `master` wasn't readable without approval. So whether it still reproduces is unconfirmed.\n\nI changed `src/ui/theme.js`, adding `nameColor(id, fallback)` and a `contrast()` helper. `nameColor()` returns the friend's normal colour; with High contrast on, it darkens it in small steps until it reaches 4.5:1 on the cream panel. Unknown speakers fall back to `C.inkSoft`. I changed `src/scenes/OutcomeScene.js`: reaction names now use it and go from size 12 to 13 (17 px on screen), and the clue recap names use it too. In `src/scenes/EndingScene.js`, the roll call names use it at 14, and so do the chat names and the names on \"The End\" card. I also added one bullet to `game/CLAUDE.md`.\n\nThe roll call sits on the book's paper rather than the cream panel, so its 4.5:1 there hasn't been measured. All three done-criteria patterns match."}
