{"at":"2026-11-24T16:26:10.520Z","round":15,"event":"write","id":"volume_default_when_empty","ok":true,"cost_usd":0.49634040000000007,"turns":8,"summary":"I fixed bug SF-04: an empty or broken saved music volume now falls back to 25% instead of muting the game. I couldn't run `npm run boot-test`, because the command needed an approval this session couldn't get, so that test is still to run. I also didn't run the bug hunter's script for SF-04, so its \"no longer reproduces\" check is unconfirmed too. The cause was in `src/ui/music.js`: an empty saved value read as 0, which silenced music and sound effects for good. The new `readSavedVolume()` only uses a real number from 0 to 1, so a saved 0 still stays silent; anything else (missing, empty, blank, not a number or out of range) gives the 25% default. The files I changed are `src/ui/music.js` and `CLAUDE.md`, where I added one bullet to \"Decisions taken in the prototype\" ending \"(feature agent, 2026-11-24)\"."}
